USB Ethernet class drivers of CherryUSB v1.6.1 (rtos/cherryusb/net): receive-path hardening only.
- rtl8152, asix, cdc_ncm: an unterminated receive that fills the buffer is dropped and the
  stream resynchronised instead of spinning forever in while (1) {} at the rx thread's priority.
- rtl8152: aggregate walk bounded by the received length (a bad descriptor or the missing
  RX_ALIGN pad after the last frame underflowed the uint32 length and read past the buffer).
- asix: same bounded walk, frames 2-byte aligned (Linux asix_rx_fixup_internal); ZLP test
  precedence fixed (!(x) % mps was always 0); rx/tx buffer sizes were swapped.
- cdc_ncm: NDP and datagram index/length checked against the received block.

diff --git a/class/cdc/usbh_cdc_ncm.c b/class/cdc/usbh_cdc_ncm.c
